  "body": "Part of #290 (design decisions D1-D10 in its research comment).\n\nDepends on: #533, #534.\n\nA constant taper angle expressed as the move pose (D2): the wire direction tilted by the angle toward the stated side. The post writes the taper the way the dialect's codes state (angle words or UV), per D5.\n\nRefusals: an angle above the machine's stated maximum (naming the op and the angle), and a UV point outside the travel band or guide reach.\n\n**Done means:** a 3° die posts and verifies, a 30° request on a 15° machine is refused by name, and the CL golden shows the poses.",
